cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: "zkp-android-spartan: Spartan proofs for e-ID on Android"
authors:
  - family-names: Dengler
    given-names: Carine
    affiliation: EPFL
  - family-names: Gasser
    given-names: Linus
    affiliation: EPFL
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23694719
repository-code: https://github.com/eid-privacy/zkp-android-spartan
license: MPL-2.0
abstract: >-
  Experimental Android app that generates and verifies zero-knowledge proofs on the phone
  with the Spartan backend for Noir over Tom-256 (eid-privacy/spartan-backend), called
  from Kotlin through UniFFI. It benchmarks proof generation (with and without
  precomputation) and verification for the e-ID circuits c0200_swiyu_jwt (age proof on a
  SWIYU SD-JWT with holder binding) and c0202_sicpa_backend_constant. These are the mobile
  numbers of the final report of the grant.
keywords:
  - zero-knowledge proofs
  - Spartan
  - Noir
  - Android
  - mobile
  - benchmarks
  - SD-JWT
  - e-ID
  - swiyu
